# REUSES THE SAME LABELS as blank_nodes.nt, on purpose.
#
# RDF 1.1: blank node labels are scoped to the document. `_:b1` here and `_:b1`
# there are DIFFERENT nodes, and loading both files must not merge them.
#
# This store makes a blank node's identity its label, forever and everywhere —
# term_uuid is a UUIDv5 over (term_text, term_type, lang, datatype_id), which
# for a blank node reduces to the label. So loading both files merges _:b1 and
# _:b3 across documents. That is the collision issues/076 facet 2 has to
# decide about, and this file is the only way to test whichever way it goes.
_:b1 <http://example.org/from_second_file> "should not merge with b1" .
_:b3 <http://example.org/from_second_file> "should not merge with b3" .
